---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const base = '/prisma-to-sql';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Verify parity - prisma-sql"
  description="Run the same read queries through Prisma and prisma-sql against one database and diff the results before adopting."
  active={`${base}/docs/verify`}
>
  <h1>Verify parity</h1>
  <p>
    <code>prisma-sql-verify</code> runs the same read queries through plain Prisma and through the speed extension on the
    same database, then diffs the results — including value types (<code>DateTime</code>, <code>BigInt</code>,
    <code>Decimal</code>) and nested include shapes. Use it before adopting and after upgrades.
  </p>

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <pre><code>{`npx prisma-sql-verify \\
  --corpus queries.jsonl \\
  --generated ./generated/sql \\
  --client @prisma/client \\
  --sqlite ./data.db

# or PostgreSQL
npx prisma-sql-verify \\
  --corpus queries.jsonl \\
  --generated ./generated/sql \\
  --client ./dist/prisma/generated/client/index.js \\
  --postgres-url $DATABASE_URL`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Corpus format</h2>
  <p>One JSON object per line. Only supported read methods are allowed.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{"model":"user","method":"findMany","args":{"take":5}}
{"model":"user","method":"findFirst","args":{"include":{"posts":true},"orderBy":{"id":"asc"}}}
{"model":"user","method":"count","args":{"where":{"status":"ACTIVE"}}}
{"model":"user","method":"aggregate","args":{"_count":true,"_avg":{"age":true}}}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Flags</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>--corpus</code></td><td>Path to the JSONL corpus file (required)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--generated</code></td><td>Generated SQL module or directory exporting speedExtension (required). Under tsx, a directory with index.ts works too.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--client</code></td><td>Module path or package name exporting PrismaClient (required)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--sqlite</code></td><td>SQLite database file to verify against</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--postgres-url</code></td><td>PostgreSQL connection string (falls back to DATABASE_URL)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--client-init</code></td><td>JSON string passed to the PrismaClient constructor. When omitted, prisma-sql-verify auto-builds a driver adapter for Prisma 7 clients (@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3 / @prisma/adapter-pg must be installed).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--verbose</code></td><td>Print passing queries too</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Exit codes and output</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>0</code> — every query matches Prisma</li>
    <li><code>1</code> — at least one mismatch; each mismatch prints the diff paths, e.g.
      <code>$.assignedTasks[0].dueDate: prisma=... extended=...</code>, ready to paste into an issue</li>
    <li><code>2</code> — usage or setup error</li>
  </ul>
  <blockquote>
    Tip: build your corpus from real application queries. A corpus of realistic shapes is worth more than a large
    synthetic one.
  </blockquote>
</DocsLayout>
